From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] panfrost: pan_cast_and_pack: the cast takes the whole pointer

pan_cast_and_pack(dst, T, name) cast "dst" without parentheses, so for
an expression the cast took only its first operand. The framebuffer
preload's padding descriptor (Bifrost: an empty ATTRIBUTE_BUFFER marks
the end of prefetching),

   pan_cast_and_pack(varying_buffer.cpu + pan_size(ATTRIBUTE_BUFFER), ...)

became (struct mali_attribute_buffer_packed *)varying_buffer.cpu + 16:
16 descriptors on, 256 bytes instead of 16, 240 bytes past the end of
the 32-byte allocation. Every preload of a framebuffer (a batch that
draws over what an earlier one left) wrote {type 1D, pointer 0} there:
over another descriptor of the pool (GPU job faults, DATA_INVALID and
reads at VA 0xc0, 0x1c0, 0x2c0: a null pointer plus an offset), and
with the allocation at the end of the pool's BO, past it (a crash in
pan_preload_emit_pre_frame_dcd from glCopyTexImage2D's blit, DOOM 3 BFG
with its 3D view resized). Parenthesize the argument.

--- a/src/panfrost/lib/genxml/pan_pack_helpers.h
+++ b/src/panfrost/lib/genxml/pan_pack_helpers.h
@@ -98,10 +98,10 @@
         }))
 
 #define pan_cast_and_pack(dst, T, name)                                        \
-   pan_pack((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)dst, T, name)
+   pan_pack((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)(dst), T, name)
 
 #define pan_cast_and_pack_nodefaults(dst, T, name)                             \
-   pan_pack_nodefaults((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)dst, T, name)
+   pan_pack_nodefaults((PREFIX2(T, PACKED_T) *)(dst), T, name)
 
 #define pan_unpack(src, T, name)                                               \
    UNUSED struct PREFIX1(T) name;                                              \
